cacti cactus prickly pears fruit crop pads paddles plants crop~
   Prickly cacti grow in loose rows across the field, each topped with a bright
purple pear. Take care, though, as these pears are as spined as the plants they
grow upon. The plants themselves are made of pale green pads, connected edge-
to-edge. It in no way resembles the tree that ordinary pears grow from.
~
